# Confirm before deleting art / shader assets

Before **deleting**, **moving to trash**, or **omitting from a refactor** any of these under `Assets/` (or equivalent project art paths), **stop and ask the user to confirm**:

| Kind | Extensions / patterns |
|------|------------------------|
| Shader Graph | `*.shadergraph`, `*.shadersubgraph` |
| Material | `*.mat` |
| Photoshop | `*.psd` |
| Aseprite | `*.aseprite` |

Include the **paired `.meta`** in the list when you would remove the asset.

## Required workflow

1. **List every path** you intend to delete (full paths, one per line).
2. **State why** (unused, replaced by USS, refactor scope, etc.).
3. **Wait for explicit approval** — e.g. “yes, delete them”, “delete shader only”, “keep Aseprite”.
4. Only then use `Delete`, `git rm`, or edits that remove the files.

## Do not

- Delete these files because a feature switched to code/USS/sprites-off without asking.
- Batch-delete “cleanup” art assets in the same turn as implementation unless the user already approved that list.
- Substitute “I removed the reference” for deleting the asset without confirmation when deletion is still on the table.

## Allowed without extra confirmation

- Removing **C# / USS references** to an asset the user asked to stop using (catalog field, sync binding) when the **files stay on disk**.
- Deleting **generated** or **clearly ephemeral** copies only if the user requested that cleanup in the same message.

## Example

> I can remove `Assets/Shaders/Graph/Map/MapCellWall.shadergraph` and `Assets/UI/Materials/MapCellWall.mat` since walls use UITK borders now. **Confirm delete these two (+ .meta)?** (Keep / delete / list only)
